  "content": {
    "id": "trig-r10-routine-7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Prove algebraically that if $n$ is a solution of the equation $3\\cos x=2-\\frac{x}{4}$, then $-4\\le n\\le20$.\n\nHint: consider the range of $\\cos n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-1\\le\\cos n\\le1$, so $-3\\le2-\\frac n4\\le3$, giving $-4\\le n\\le20$.",
      "worked": "Since $n$ is a solution, $3\\cos n=2-\\frac n4$. Using the range of cosine,\n$$\\begin{align*}-1&\\le\\cos n\\le1\\\\-3&\\le3\\cos n\\le3\\\\-3&\\le2-\\frac n4\\le3\\\\-5&\\le-\\frac n4\\le1\\\\20&\\ge n\\ge-4.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $-4\\le n\\le20$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
